   "body": "## Goal\nTask #352 added a synthetic populated manifest and a runner contract, merged at f405d54: benchmark/baseline/run-manifest.synthetic.json (sha256 4d4c2b0f...), benchmark/scripts/runner_contract.py (f5f1b174...), benchmark/baseline/runner-contract.md (b9e47205...). They are not pinned in benchmark/preparation.json. Give an independent Spec and Standards verdict before the Policymaker pins them.\n\nExpected gain: a reviewed runner contract lets the Policymaker pin it under the baseline milestone, which closes gap N3. The next Policymaker reads the verdict (accept/revise) and numbered findings with file:line pointers in this report.\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] Write `.session/report.md` in your first turns and update it. Report only: do not edit repository files.\n- [ ] Spec: compare the manifest field names and null reasons with benchmark/baseline/run-manifest.template.json by script (all names present, no extras, every null keeps the template reason, every populated value is marked synthetic).\n- [ ] Spec: check the run plan (cases x arms x repetitions) against benchmark/protocol.md `## baseline` (arms, repetitions, order randomisation). Check that run_record.py is imported unchanged and that `validate` and `bind_manifest` are really called per record.\n- [ ] Probes in a temporary copy (not in the repository): remove one mutation's expected-reason comparison, make the audit ignore a missing run, accept a record bound to another manifest, and edit the synthetic manifest by one byte. Each must make `--check` exit nonzero; report each result.\n- [ ] Honesty: runner-contract.md must say design only, no runs, no readiness, tool quality unmeasured, and name the open resource rows #169/#268.\n- [ ] Verdict `accept` (no blocking findings) or `revise` (numbered blocking findings, each with an exact fix). Report your actual model family; the author was Claude Sonnet.\n\n## Verification\n`python3 -I -B benchmark/scripts/runner_contract.py --check`\n\n## Context\n